  "narrative": "I now have sufficient evidence to write the narrative. The enrichment clearly identifies tryptophan metabolism as the dominant affected pathway, and I have verified the L-Tryptophan → Serotonin → Melatonin upstream path.\n\n---\n\n**Narrative**\n\nThe most strongly enriched pathway in this dataset is **Tryptophan metabolism (KEGG map00380)** — FDR 0.0, fold enrichment ~600× — with six matched compounds: L-Tryptophan (C00078), Tryptamine (C00398), Indoleacetaldehyde (C00637), 3-Hydroxyanthranilic acid (C00632), Serotonin (C00780), and Melatonin (C01598). A closely related Reactome module, **Serotonin and melatonin biosynthesis (R-HSA-209931)**, is also hit with the highest fold enrichment in the analysis (>1,000×), confirming that the biosynthetic arm of tryptophan metabolism is the primary affected system.\n\n**Key drivers.** L-Tryptophan (C00078) is the pathway entry point and clear upstream driver. KEGG graph traversal confirms it is 2 hops upstream of Serotonin (via 5-hydroxytryptophan) and 4 hops upstream of Melatonin (via Serotonin → N-acetylserotonin → Melatonin), establishing a verified directional cascade. The coordinated elevation of L-Tryptophan, Serotonin, and Melatonin together is therefore consistent with increased flux through the indoleamine biosynthetic route rather than a block at a single step. Tryptamine and Indoleacetaldehyde, which represent the decarboxylation/aldehyde arm of tryptophan catabolism, likely reflect parallel activation of that branch.\n\n**Biological significance.** Dysregulation of the tryptophan–serotonin–melatonin axis has broad physiological relevance. Serotonin modulates mood, cognition, and gastrointestinal motility; Melatonin governs circadian rhythm and抗氧化 response; 3-Hydroxyanthranilic acid sits at the intersection of tryptophan metabolism and the kynurenine pathway, linking this signature to immune activation and oxidative stress. Together, the pattern suggests the treatment condition drives tryptophan toward the indoleamine arms of its metabolism, with downstream consequences for neuroendocrine signaling and possibly inflammatory tone.\n\n*Verified upstream relationships: L-Tryptophan (C00078) → Serotonin (C00780) → Melatonin (C01598).*",
